# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# Local configuration. `.env.example` is deliberately NOT ignored — it is the
# documentation and must be committed.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# ⚠ Editor swap and backup files, and this entry is not tidiness. A `.env.swp`
# holds the BUFFER of the file it belongs to, so ignoring `.env` while leaving
# its swap file tracked publishes the contents anyway. One was caught in a
# commit on 2026-09-07 by reading the `git show --stat` output; `git add -A` had
# swept it in exactly as it once swept in the runtime database.
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn
*~
.*.sw[a-p]

# Runtime state. DB_PATH and PHOTOS_DIR default under data/, so simply running
# the binary from the repository root creates these — which is how the database
# and a directory of uploaded photographs got committed once already.
data/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/
